question:
In the classic ABCDE model of flower development, different combinations of ABCDE class genes result
in different whorls of organs. Which one of the following models would likely give rise to unisexual
flower structures?
In the ABCDE model,
class A + E genes specify sepals;
class A + B + E genes, petals;
class B + C + E genes, stamens;
class C + E genes, carpels; and
class C + D + E genes, ovules.
Source: Fundamental and Practice, Life Sciences - 2
